  "question": {
    "text": "The power factor of an L-R series circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and that of a C-R series circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. If the elements <math><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,&nbsp;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of the two circuits are joined in series and connected to the same ac source, the power factor of this circuit is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. The ratio of the resistance in the L-R circuit to the resistance in the C-R circuit is"
  },
